### Module Structure

All C++ code lives in namespace `RUBIDIUM`. Module sub-namespaces have been eliminated — classes from `shell/`, `canvas/`, `updater/` live directly in `namespace RUBIDIUM`. Sneeze types use `SNEEZE::CORE::`, `SNEEZE::renderer::`, etc. Source files are under `src/`:

| Module | Namespace | Purpose | Status |
|--------|-----------|---------|--------|
| `shell/` | `RUBIDIUM` | Application controller and native window frames. Abstract base class `APP` (`App.h`/`App.cpp`) owns cross-platform concerns: `SNEEZE::IENGINE` host interface, settings management (loads/saves `settings.json`, formerly standalone `SETTINGS` singleton), SDL window registry (`ISDLWINDOW` map + `SDLWindow_Translate` dispatch), `LOGGER` ownership, font family. Platform-derived class `APPNATIVE` (`App_Win32.h`/`App_Win32.cpp` on Windows) owns platform-specific concerns: single-instance mutex, WNDCLASSEXW registration, Win32 message pump (`EventLoop`), `IAPPWINDOW` implementation (window create/destroy/focus/blur/new/exit callbacks), DPI awareness, Sneeze engine lifecycle. `IAPPWINDOW` callback interface (formerly `IAPPFRAME`) decouples window lifecycle events from `APPFRAME`. Multi-window: `APPNATIVE::Impl` maintains `std::vector<APPFRAME*>`, creates windows via `Window_Create()`, terminates when last window closes. Abstract base `APPFRAME` with `ProcessInput()` pure virtual; single concrete class name `APPFRAME_NATIVE` per platform. Non-Windows platforms inherit from `APPFRAME_SDL` (intermediate base). | Active — **stable, working** |
| `canvas/` | `RUBIDIUM` | SDL3 rendering viewport — borderless SDL window reparented as `WS_CHILD` of APPFRAME's viewport region. No longer owns the top-level window. | Active |
| `astro/` | `RUBIDIUM` | Orbital mechanics, solar system body data (disposable demo) | Temporary — will be removed as browser progresses |
| `updater/` | `RUBIDIUM` | Slim update interface — checks for staged updates, prompts user, spawns RubidiumSetup.exe, polls for force-check results | Active |
| `rmlui_sdl/` | `RUBIDIUM` | Reusable RmlUi/SDL3 window module. `RMLUI_SDL` class implements `ISDLWINDOW` and encapsulates all SDL window + RmlUi context boilerplate. Two-phase init: `Initialize(sTitle, nWidth, nHeight)` creates infrastructure (with `SDL_WINDOW_HIGH_PIXEL_DENSITY`, sets DPI ratios) and registers with `APP::SDLWindow_Register()`; `LoadDocument(sRmlDocument)` loads a fully-prepared RML string. Event handling: `HandleEvent(SDL_Event&)` routes to RmlUi input handler then calls `Render()` for immediate repaint; `Render()` runs `Context::Update()` + `Context::Render()` only when visible. Also handles `SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_MOVED` and `SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_RESIZED` (fired once upon completion of move/resize) — invokes optional `FN_WINDOW_GEOMETRY` callback with current x, y, width, height. `SetPosition(int nX, int nY)` sets window position via `SDL_SetWindowPosition`. `SetGeometryCallback(FN_WINDOW_GEOMETRY, void*)` registers an optional callback for geometry change notifications. Destructor unregisters from SDL window registry. DPI handled automatically. Used via composition (`RMLUI_SDL m_Window` member). Consumers: `INSPECTOR_RML`, `UrlBarRml` (future). | Active — **shared infrastructure** |
| `inspector/` | `RUBIDIUM` | Developer tools panel — two implementations coexist during migration. **Old Inspector** (`Inspector.h/.cpp`, `Tab_*.cpp`): Win32 native popup with 8 tabs, Network tab fully implemented with live file table, toolbar, filters, container sidebar, timing waterfall. Toggled via F12 or ellipsis menu "Old Inspector". **New Inspector** (`InspectorRml.h/.cpp`, `network/`): Cross-platform RmlUi/SDL3 popup, pixel-perfect Chromium-style layout. Uses `RMLUI_SDL` via composition for window management. Widget hierarchy: `INSPECTOR_WIDGET` base class (virtual `Id()`, `Initialize(Rml::Element*)`, static `Create()` factory), `IW_` prefix naming convention (e.g., `IW_NETWORK`, `IW_NETWORK_TOOLBAR`). Each tab panel is an `INSPECTOR_WIDGET` subclass with its own `_Frame.cpp`. Network tab compartmentalized into separate C++ classes per component. Table-driven child widget instantiation via `FN_CREATEWIDGET` arrays and loops. Toggled via F11 or ellipsis menu "New Inspector". Starts hidden. All tab headers consolidated into single `Tab.h`. | Active — **migrating to RmlUi** |
| `settings/` | `RUBIDIUM` | **REMOVED (absorbed into APP base class).** Application settings (app data path resolution, `settings.json` load/save, centralized preferences access) now live directly in the `APP` base class. The standalone `SETTINGS` singleton and `src/settings/` directory no longer exist. Access pattern changed from `SETTINGS::GetInstance()->JSON()` to `APPNATIVE::GetInstance()->SettingToJSON()`. | Removed |
| `logger/` | (global) | Logging infrastructure — `ILOGGER` (abstract output interface), `ILOGGER_NATIVE` (platform backend: `printf` on Windows, `SDL_Log` elsewhere), `LOGGER` (threaded log processor with timestamped, leveled, module-tagged output). Owned by `APP`, pointer passed to `APPFRAME`s and modules. | Active |

### Key Classes

| Class | Module | Purpose |
|-------|--------|---------|
| `APP` | `shell` | Abstract base class (`App.h`/`App.cpp`) — the cross-platform application foundation. Inherits from `SNEEZE::IENGINE` (engine host interface). NOT a singleton — platform-derived class provides that. Constructor takes `(std::string sHomePath, ILOGGER* pILogger)`: resolves app data path, creates `Metaversal/Rubidium/` directories, loads `settings.json` (with `merge_patch` against defaults so all keys exist), creates `LOGGER` from the provided backend. Destructor writes `settings.json` to disk and destroys logger. Pure virtual `Run()`. Responsibilities: (1) **Settings management** (formerly `SETTINGS` singleton) — `SettingToJSON()` returns mutable `nlohmann::json&`; `sHomePath()` returns the resolved app data directory. (2) **IENGINE host** — `sAppDataPath()` returns `m_sHomePath`, `sRenderer()` returns `"halogen"`, `Log()` delegates to `m_pLogger`. (3) **SDL window registry** — `SDLWindow_Register(ISDLWINDOW*)` / `SDLWindow_Unregister(ISDLWINDOW*)` manage `m_mapSDLWindow` (unordered_map keyed by `SDL_WindowID`); `SDLWindow_Translate(SDL_Event&)` extracts the window ID from any SDL event type and dispatches to the matching `ISDLWINDOW::HandleEvent()`. (4) **Font family** — `sFontFamily()` getter, `sFontFamily(string)` setter. (5) **Logger** — `Logger()` accessor; `DestroyLogger()` for safe teardown ordering (derived class calls it from its dtor before deleting the ILOGGER backend). |
| `APPNATIVE` | `shell` | Win32 platform-derived class (`App_Win32.h`/`App_Win32.cpp`). Inherits `APP`. Meyers singleton via `APPNATIVE::GetInstance()`. Constructor: calls `APP(ResolveAppDataPath(), new ILOGGER_NATIVE())`, creates `Impl`. `Impl` inherits `IAPPWINDOW` and owns all Win32-specific state: single-instance mutex, `HINSTANCE`, `HACCEL`, `SNEEZE::ENGINE*`, `std::vector<APPFRAME*> m_apAppFrame`, active/last-active window pointers. `Impl::Run()`: DPI awareness, WNDCLASSEXW registration, common controls init, log level restore from settings, Sneeze engine creation, font family resolution (`WINUTILS::DefaultFontFamily`/`FontFilePath`), `Rml::LoadFontFace`, `SDL_Init`, initial window creation, enters `EventLoop`. `Impl::EventLoop()`: Win32 message pump (`PeekMessageA` + accelerator dispatch), then `SDL_PollEvent` loop calling `m_pApp->SDLWindow_Translate(Event)` for each event, then `pAppFrame->ProcessInput()` for ALL AppFrames (not just active — ensures scroll deltas reach unfocused viewports), then `MsgWaitForMultipleObjects(INFINITE)` to sleep until next input. `IAPPWINDOW` callbacks: `Window_OnCreate` (reads geometry from settings or source window), `Window_OnDestroy` (saves geometry on last-close, posts quit), `Window_OnFocus/Blur`, `Window_OnNew`, `Window_OnExit` (posts WM_CLOSE to all). |
| `ISDLWINDOW` | `shell` | Interface for SDL window event dispatch (`App.h`). Two pure virtuals: `SDLWindowID() const` (returns the SDL window ID for event routing) and `HandleEvent(SDL_Event&)` (processes a single dispatched event). Implemented by `CANVAS` and `RMLUI_SDL`. Windows register/unregister with `APP::SDLWindow_Register`/`Unregister` during their init/teardown. The central event loop drains `SDL_PollEvent` once per frame and calls `APP::SDLWindow_Translate` for each event — no competing poll loops, no events consumed by the wrong window. |
