| 2 | Auto-updater | **DONE.** All three modes tested end-to-end (fresh install, background check, apply). All three prompt responses verified (Install, Skip, Cancel). Stale staged/skipped cleanup working. Force check via Ctrl+Shift+U with inline result detection (no-update dialog or update prompt). Settings.json created on first launch with defaults. |
| 3 | Browser chrome framework | **IN PROGRESS.** `APP` (`src/shell/App.h/.cpp`) is the application controller — owns the window lifecycle, Sneeze host interface (`ISNEEZE`), and Win32 message pump. `IAPPFRAME` callback interface decouples window lifecycle events from `APPFRAME`. **Multi-window support:** `APP` maintains `std::vector<APPFRAME_NATIVE*>`, creates windows via `Window_Create()`, tracks the active (focused) window, and terminates when the last window closes. Window geometry (position, size, maximized) saved on last-window-close and restored on next launch. Ellipsis menu includes "New Window" and "New Incognito Window" items (mapped to `SNEEZE::VIEWPORT::kPERSISTENT` / `kTRANSITORY`). "Exit" closes all open windows. `APPFRAME_NATIVE` implements DWM custom title bar, pill-shaped URL bar, app icon, account icon, vertical ellipsis menu. SDL rendering embedded as edge-to-edge child viewport. Full DPI awareness (per-monitor v2). Window resizable from all edges/corners via child subclassing for `HTTRANSPARENT`. DWM system caption buttons used by default; custom-drawn buttons available via `#ifdef RUBIDIUM_CUSTOM_CAPTION_BUTTONS`. Toolbar button hover on mouseover. Win32 implementation stable and working. Single-instance mutex prevents duplicate processes. |
| 4 | Settings / preferences UI | User-facing configuration |
| 5 | Authenticode code signing | EV certificate required to eliminate Windows SmartScreen "unknown publisher" warning. Sign both `Rubidium.exe` and the NSIS installer with `signtool.exe`. Needed before any public release. |
| 6 | macOS code signing | Apple requires code signing and notarization for distribution. Needs Apple Developer account, `codesign`, and `notarytool`. |
| 7 | Cross-platform build and test | Build, test, and run on macOS and Linux. Verify CMake, CPack, and runtime on each platform. |
| 8 | GPU-accelerated ANARI device | **DONE.** Halogen (Filament-based) GPU-accelerated ANARI device integrated. Replaced Helide CPU ray tracer. DLL: `anari_library_halogen.dll` from `SNEEZE_LIBS_DIR/Halogen/install/bin/`. Renderer name: `"halogen"`. Sneeze-side: directional light (irradiance 3.0) + ambient light (radiance 0.2) — Filament is PBR and requires explicit lighting unlike Helide. CPU usage dropped from ~84% to ~4.5%. Helide has since been removed from the Sneeze dep build entirely (`BUILD_HELIDE_DEVICE=OFF`). |
| 9 | WASM debug console windows | Each WASM container gets a separate debug console window for logs. Developers see a tree view of fabrics/services and can open debug consoles per container (multiple simultaneously). Not for this phase — deferred until the main application frame is stable and the console window is replaced. Needs investigation: Win32 `AllocConsole` only supports one console per process, so will likely need custom Win32 windows with rich text controls, or a developer tools panel within the native frame. |
| 10 | MSF/MSS file formats and JWS trust model | **DESIGNED.** Full architectural spec written for MSF (fabric descriptor) and MSS (service descriptor) file formats — JWS-signed (RFC 7515) with X.509 code signing certificate chains (`x5c`). Trust model: certificate-based identity (domain-independent), container isolation (persona + signing key fingerprint + namespace), tiered storage (persona > certificate > namespace), certificate rotation via succession declarations. Paper: `MSF-MSS.md`. AI context: `MSF-MSS.mdc`. JWS implementation handoff: `JWS.mdc`. All three files created in Rubidium repo for convenience, to be relocated to Sneeze or another project for implementation. Recommended library: jwt-cpp (header-only, MIT, OpenSSL, nlohmann/json). Implementation is a Sneeze-side task. |
| 11 | Build system restructuring | **DONE.** Migrated from single SuperBuild `CMakeLists.txt` to two independent CMake trees (`deps/` and `src/`) mirroring Sneeze's architecture. Platform build scripts (`scripts/build-windows.ps1`, `scripts/build-{linux,macos,deps}.sh`) are the only glue. Stamp-cached deps. Shared source clones. Per-platform per-config isolation. Old top-level `CMakeLists.txt` and `scripts/build.{ps1,sh}` deleted. Release build verified working on Windows. |
| 13 | Cache inspector (Network tab) | **DONE (Phases 1–4) — now migrating to cross-platform RmlUi.** Original Win32 native implementation: Chrome DevTools-style Network panel in `src/inspector/`. Live file table, toolbar with Record/Stop/Clear/Reset/Filter/Disable Cache, text and type filters, container sidebar, right-click context menu, timing waterfall with color-coded bars, and detail pane (Headers/Preview/Response/Timing tabs). Wired to Sneeze cache API via `FILE::Request()` / `FILE::Release()` attach/detach lifecycle for detail pane data access. Tab system with 8 tabs (Network active, others placeholder). Window position and column widths persisted. **Future enhancements considered:** interactive time-range selector on waterfall (Chrome-style grabbers that filter the list to a time window), queue-phase visualization in waterfall bars, retention window setting (inspector sends policy to cache manager, which prunes and fires `OnCacheFileDeleted` — important for long-lived metaverse sessions vs. web page loads). |
| 14 | Cross-platform inspector (RmlUi migration) | **IN PROGRESS.** Replacing the Win32 native inspector with a cross-platform RmlUi/SDL3 implementation. **Architecture (current as of 2026-05-31):** `INSPECTOR_RML::Impl` uses `RMLUI_SDL` via composition (`m_Window` member) — all SDL/RmlUi window boilerplate extracted into the reusable `src/rmlui_sdl/` module. `Impl` inherits `Rml::EventListener` for tab click dispatch and `Rml::EventId::Keydown` for global keyboard shortcuts (Ctrl+F for Elements search). Owns `m_apTab[kTAB_COUNT]` + `m_nActiveTab` for tracking the currently active tab. Static members: `s_afnCreateWidget[]` factory table, `s_sRmlStyle` (CSS from `.inl` file, all `dp` units + `1px` borders), `s_sRmlDocument` (RML template with single `[{STYLE}]` placeholder). Initialize flow: read stored geometry from `settings.json["inspector_rml"]` → `m_Window.Initialize()` with stored/default size → `SetPosition()` if stored → `SetGeometryCallback()` → substitute `[{FONT-FAMILY}]` + `[{STYLE}]` → `m_Window.LoadDocument()` → create tabs in loop. DPI scaling fully automatic via `RMLUI_SDL` (`SetDensityIndependentPixelRatio` + `SDL_WINDOW_HIGH_PIXEL_DENSITY`). Window geometry persisted on every completed move/resize via `FN_WINDOW_GEOMETRY` callback. Each `INSPECTOR_TAB` owns an `INSPECTOR_WIDGET*` (polymorphic base class defined in `InspectorRml.h`). Widget classes use `IW_` prefix naming. **Tabs implemented:** Network (fully implemented with all sub-components), Console (toolbar with Clear/Filter/Levels/Settings + 3-line settings tray, containers sidebar, entries placeholder), Elements (tree area with path bar + collapsible Ctrl+F search bar, details panel with Computed/Details/Events sub-tabs), Storage (renamed from Application — containers sidebar, preview pane with 5 custom tabs + toolbar with search/clear/delete), Security (containers sidebar, preview placeholder with shield icon), Performance (toolbar with Record/Clear, metrics dashboard cards for FPS/Frame/Submit/Render, chart placeholder, scrollable log area with JetBrains Mono). **Stubs remaining:** Sources, Memory. Each widget has `static Create()` factory, virtual `Id()` (returns e.g. `"network"`), virtual `Initialize(Rml::Element* pContainer)`. Composite widgets use table-driven child instantiation: `enum eWIDGET` + `static const FN_CREATEWIDGET s_afnCreateWidget[]` + base class `CreateWidgets()` helper. Each widget defines its own static RML string (`s_sRml` as `R"rml(...)rml"` raw string literals) injected via `SetInnerRML()`. Base class `INSPECTOR_WIDGET` owns `m_pContainer`, `std::vector<INSPECTOR_WIDGET*> m_apChildren`, provides `Container()`, `Container(int)`, `Widget(int)` accessors, destructor handles child cleanup. Shared CSS in `InspectorRml_Style.inl` uses generic reusable classes: `panel-toolbar`, `panel-body`, `panel-sidebar`, `panel-main`, `panel-statusbar`, `panel-tabbar`, `panel-content`, `panel-bottombar`, `panel-searchbar`, `split-left`/`split-right`, `perf-metrics`/`metric-card`/`perf-chart`/`perf-log`. Common `IW_BUTTON` class (in `src/inspector/common/Button.h`) with static factory methods for standard icons (Record, Clear, Settings, Filter, Delete). Nomenclature: tab buttons are `id="tab-<name>"`, content areas are `id="panel-<name>"`. File structure: each panel in its own subfolder (`elements/`, `network/`, `console/`, `storage/`, `security/`, `performance/`, etc.) with header + `*_Frame.cpp`. Network files prefixed `Network_` to avoid MSVC `.obj` collisions. Pixel-perfect Chromium DevTools color scheme. Both inspectors coexist: F11 / "New Inspector" for RmlUi, F12 / "Old Inspector" for Win32 native. Not yet wired to Sneeze cache events. **Fonts:** Inter (UI text), Material Symbols Outlined (icons), JetBrains Mono (monospace/log) — managed as build-time dependencies via `deps/fonts.cmake`. **Next:** (1) Wire cache data, implement toolbar actions, populate file list with live data. (2) Build horizontal waterfall. (3) Implement detail pane content. (4) Wire Performance tab to Sneeze telemetry. (5) Wire Console tab to logger output. Future: reusable component library and multi-DPI validation. |
| 15 | Hand-maintained MSVC projects | **DONE.** Created `msvc/Rubidium.sln`, `Rubidium.vcxproj`, `Rubidium.vcxproj.filters` for Rubidium; `Sneeze/msvc/Sneeze.sln`, `Sneeze.vcxproj`, `Sneeze.vcxproj.filters` for Sneeze; `Sneeze/msvc/SneezeTest.vcxproj` + `.filters` for Sneeze tests. Rubidium solution references all three projects. MSBuild macros for portable relative paths. PCH via `pch.cpp`/`Pch.cpp`. Version header via PowerShell PreBuildEvent. AI-driven `sync-build` skill in both repos for `.vcxproj` → `CMakeLists.txt` synchronization. Both Debug and Release configs build and run successfully. |
| 12 | Multi-config Rubidium tree | **DONE.** Rubidium's per-config build tree collapsed into a single multi-config CMake tree at `builds/<platform>/build/` (VS/Xcode on IDE platforms, Ninja Multi-Config on Linux/macOS CLI). One `Rubidium.sln` per platform, toolbar dropdown flips Debug/Release and both build against their respective per-config deps tree without reconfigure. Per-config install trees at `builds/<platform>/install/{debug,release}/{bin,pkg}/`. Deps trees stay per-config as before. `CMAKE_CONFIGURATION_TYPES` pinned to `Debug;Release` to keep CMake from probing deps paths that don't exist. Sneeze-side path generalization rewrites imported targets across `anari::anari_static` + `vox::vox` with a `_resolve_variant` helper that handles Debug-suffix filenames (`libcurl-d.lib`, `openxr_loaderd.lib`, `spirv-cross-cored.lib`). Rubidium-side does the same for SDL3. CPack output chosen at CPack time by `CPackProjectConfig.cmake` reading `CPACK_BUILD_CONFIG`. |
